return {
["20:00"]={"It’s the twenty-third of June nineteen seventy-five, and it is \003eight o’clock\004 in the evening, seated at his jigsaw puzzle, Bartlebooth has just died.","Life: A User’s Manual","Georges Perec"},
["20:01"]={"It was only \003a little after eight o’clock\004, so all the shows were about silliness or murder.","Slaughterhouse 5","Kurt Vonnegut"},
["20:02"]={"Yes, I must go to the railway station, and if he’s not there, then go there and catch him. Anna looked at the railway timetable in the newspapers. An evening train went at \003two minutes past eight\004. “Yes, I shall be in time.”","Anna Karenina","Leo Tolstoy"},
["20:03"]={"I might talk to the GP about getting some sleeping pills. I noticed that my watch had stopped at \003three minutes past eight\004, and I wondered if that was the exact time our baby died.","Rock Paper Scissors","Alice Feeny"},
["20:04"]={"The earth seems to cast its darkness upward into the air. The farm country is somber at night. He is grateful when the lights of Lankaster merge with his dim beams. He stops at a diner who’s clock says \0038:04\004.","Rabbit, Run","John Updike"},
["20:05"]={"Well, it’s \003five-past eight\004 now, I said to Drake. “You’d better go straight off and organise a flashing party. There’s not a hope of a sortie tonight at sea, but we’d better be on the safe side.”","Eight Hours from England","Anthony Quayle"},
["20:06"]={"It was \003six minutes past eight\004 when I arrived at the lighthouse. I was unable to gain entry. The door was locked.","The Lighthouse","P.D. James"},
["20:07"]={"Bennie pulled the transcripts for that night. The first call had come in at \0038:07\004, with a positive ID.","Mistaken Identity","Lisa Scottoline"},
["20:08"]={"Monday \0038:08 P.M.\004\nHe glanced at his watch, then looked out his smudgy hotel window and down at the Strand. Two more minutes and there should be a knock on the door.","Project Daedalus","Thomas Hoover"},
["20:09"]={"I have been drunk just twice in my life, and the second time was that afternoon; so everything that happened has a dim, hazy cast over it, although until \003after eight o’clock\004 the apartment was full of cheerful sun.","The Great Gatsby","F. Scott Fitzgerald"},
["20:10"]={"It is \003ten minutes past eight\004. I must tell you how much I love you at ten minutes past eight on a Sunday evening, January 27th 1918.","Letter to John Middleton Murry","Katherine Mansfield"},
["20:11"]={"The Hurleys arrived at \003eleven minutes past eight\004 precisely. When I opened the front door, Martin pushed Paige, nearly seven months pregnant and large, into the hall.\n“Thought you could do with some early back-up,” he murmured, as Nathan unwrapped Paige from her coat.","The Second Wife","Elizabeth Buchan"},
["20:13"]={"\0038:13 P.M.\004\nWhat a day! When Ally finally settled onto her couch, after giving Knickers a long walk, she was exhausted. She leaned back and kicked off her shoes. There had been a few moments of tightness in her chest—maybe it was psychological, anxiety‑induced—but that was gone now.","Syndrome","Thomas Hoover"},
["20:14"]={"When a call came through to Dilworth’s home number at \003fourteen minutes past eight\004 o’clock, Olbier and Jones reacted with far more excitement than the situation warranted because they were desperate for action.","Watchers","Dean Koontz"},
["20:15"]={"By \0038:15\004 on Sunday night Theresa had finished the last of her long-deferred homework and thought she could safely put away her arithmetic book and tell her father she was tired and ready for bed.","Devices and Desires","P.D. James"},
["20:16"]={"He kissed her hand and after a while went to get two more drinks. When he got back, it was \003sixteen minutes past eight\004, and Lois was humming softly along with the jukebox","The Rotters’ Club","Jonathan Coe"},
["20:17"]={"\00320:17\004 A red warning light failed to go on in the Drive Room, beginning a chain of events which would lead, in a further twenty-three minutes, to the total annihilation of the entire crew of Red Dwarf.","Red Dwarf","Grant Naylor"},
["20:18"]={"\0032018 hrs\004 Katya has arrived at the Odessa Hotel. Barley and Katya are talking in the canteen. Wicklow and one irregular observing. More.","The Russia House","John le Carré"},
["20:19"]={"At \0038:19\004 she received a second phone call to let her know the plane had taken off from Amman with the “cargo” on board.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
["20:20"]={"Again the boy knocked. Again there was no response. Gabriel watched and suffered with him until, at \003twenty past eight\004, the boy finally gave up and turned away.","The Mistletoe Murder","P.D. James"},
["20:21"]={"At \0038:21\004, after a knock at the door, a constable said a military police vehicle had just driven into the courtyard, the driver asking for “Mr.” Murray.","The Ipcress File","Len Deighton"},
["20:23"]={"\00320:23\004. In a few minutes she would go down. She could have borrowed some mascara from her daughter Sally, but it was too late. She could have rung her mother in Northam, but it was too late. Seven minutes of solitude she had, and then she would descend.","The Radiant Way","Margaret Drabble"},
["20:24"]={"Peach checked his watch. \0038:24.\004 If he wasn’t in a taxi in twenty minutes he’d be done for.","Dreams of Leaving","Rupert Thomson"},
["20:25"]={"She sat down in her usual seat and smiled at her husband as he sank into his own chair opposite her. She was saved. It was only \003five and twenty past eight\004.","The Listerdale Mystery","Agatha Christie"},
["20:26"]={"It was \003twenty-six minutes past eight\004. Without hesitation he went to the cloakroom, and, producing a ticker, was handed a large valise, a rug, and a thick long ulster of dark tweed.","The Temptress","William Le Quex"},
["20:27"]={"Her sister was as loyal as the day was long. There was no way she would have left the spot where they were supposed to meet, not with the sirens screaming. And so it was that she had been stuck there when another unearthly sound had ripped over the crowd’s heads at \0038:27 p.m.\004","The Little Wartime Library","Kate Thompson"},
["20:28"]={"Still seated, Haver looked up at the clock and said out of the blue: “My father died exactly twenty-five years ago.”\nLindell looked up. “Exactly?”\n“Yes, exactly. \003Twenty-eight minutes past eight\004, on this exact date twenty-five years ago.”","Stone Coffin","Kjell Eriksson"},
["20:29"]={"At \0038:29\004 I punched the front doorbell in Elgin Crescent. It was opened by a small oriental woman in a white apron. She showed me into a large, empty sitting room with an open fire and a couple of huge oil paintings.","Engleby","Sebastian Faulks"},
["20:30"]={"By \003eight-thirty\004, with dusk growing too thick to be much different from night, the five searchers had grown to a dozen.","The Tommyknockers","Stephen King"},
["20:31"]={"The time display read \00320:31\004 on the same evening. Almost dusk. The scene was motionless save the soft rustling of leaves, but the rumble of a car engine and the crunch of tires on gravel must have triggered the recording.","None So Blind","Barbara Fradkin"},
["20:32"]={"At the station he captured Miss Lantry out of the gadding mob at \003eight thirty-two\004. “We mustn’t keep mamma and the others waiting,” said she. “To Wallack’s Theatre as fast as you can drive!”","The Four Million","O. Henry"},
["20:33"]={"\00320:33\004 Navigation officer Henri DuBois knocked his black cona coffee with four sugars over his computer console keyboard. As he mopped up the coffee, he noticed three red warning blips on his monitor screen, which he wrongly assumed were the result of his spillage.","Red Dwarf","Grant Naylor"},
["20:34"]={"He wrote: “Cough (hacking): \00320:34\004 (Duration: 24 seconds)”","The Bells","Richard Harvell"},
["20:35"]={"Left Munich at \0038:35 p.m.\004 on 1st May, arriving at Vienna early the next morning","Dracula","Bram Stoker"},
["20:36"]={"\00320:36\004 Rimmer stood in the main wash-room on the stasis deck and combed his hair.","Red Dwarf","Grant Naylor"},
["20:37"]={"Pierce got to his feet and took his watch from his waistcoat, an incongruously clean gold object at the end of a soot-black chain. He snapped it open: it was \0038:37\004.","The Great Train Robbery","Michael Crichton"},
["20:38"]={"And at \003twenty-two minutes to nine\004, at the beginning of the third act, he stood up and, trying not to make too much noise, left the auditorium and walked up to the second floor.","While the Women Are Sleeping","Javier Marais"},
["20:39"]={"\0038:39 P.M.\004\nCally was thinking about how much she would love a pizza, heavy on the cheese and Italian sausage. No, just heavy on the cholesterol. Why was it that the only things that tasted good were all supposed to be bad for you?","Project Cyclops","Thomas Hoover"},
["20:40"]={"On the seventeenth. That was so. They were seated at \003twenty minutes to nine\004. It’s a little foible of mine, to note the time the customer is actually seated.","A Taste for Death","P.D. James"},
["20:41"]={"It’s \00308:41\004 and I’m in Bed practicing. Ma’s filled a plastic bag with really hot water and tied it tight so none spills out, she puts it in another bag and ties that too.","Room","Emma Donoghue"},
["20:42"]={"The hand at this moment pointed to \0038:42\004. The players took up their cards, but their eyes were constantly on the clock. One may safely say that, however secure they might feel, never had minutes seemed so long to them.","Around the World in Eighty Days","Jules Verne"},
["20:43"]={"‘\0038:43\004,’ said Thomas Flanagan, as he cut the cards placed before him by Gauthier Ralph. There was a moment’s pause, during which the spacious room was perfectly silent.","Around the World in Eighty Days","Jules Verne"},
["20:44"]={"The clock’s pendulum beat every second with mathematical regularity, and each player could count every sixtieth of a minute as it struck his ear. “\0038:44\004!” said John Sullivan, in a voice that betrayed his emotion. Only one minute more and the wager would be won.","Around the World in Eighty Days","Jules Verne"},
["20:45"]={"At \003eight forty-five\004, I called and said, “I need some financial advice. Actually, I’m serious. I’m in a bind.”","My Year of Rest and Relaxation","Ottessa Moshfegh"},
["20:46"]={"At the tone, the time will be \003eight forty six\004, exactly. One cubic mile of seawater contains about 50 pounds of gold.","Macedonia","Tom Lichtenberg"},
["20:47"]={"It read \00320:47\004 on the cooker clock when Fliss heard the jangle of Ben’s keys in the door. Somewhere along the line, her husband had stopped making any effort.","All That Is Left of Us","Catherine Miller"},
["20:48"]={"It only wants \003twelve minutes to nine\004, Constance pointed out. “Well, what if it does?”","The Old Wives’ Tale","Arnold Bennett"},
["20:49"]={"At \0038:49\004 there was a loud rap on the door, and Sir Hamish muttered an inaudible reproach as David Heath went to open it. He found his contact standing there.","A Matter of Principle","Jeffrey Archer"},
["20:50"]={"What did it mean by beginning to tick so loudly all of a sudden? Its face indicated \003ten minutes to nine\004. Mrs Verloc cared nothing for time, and the ticking went on.","The Secret Agent","Joseph Conrad"},
["20:51"]={"I stayed watching the polestar from \003nine minutes to nine\004 until ten past, tilting my head back till it hurt, fighting off dizziness and not taking my eyes off the distant, twinkling light which is our rendezvous in the sky, trying to see your face looking back at me.","Belle du Seigneur","Albert Cohen"},
